3-Bin Mapping (with detailed guidance):
1: Unresponsive / Abnormal (scores 1-3)
   - No response to painful stimuli (Score 1) OR
   - Abnormal extension (decerebrate) (Score 2): arms extended and internally rotated; legs extended; plantar flexion; suggests brainstem involvement OR
   - Abnormal flexion (decorticate) (Score 3): arms flexed and adducted; legs extended; clenched fists; suggests damage above brainstem
