2: Withdraws / Localizes (scores 4-5)
   - Withdrawal to pain (Score 4): reflexive pulling away from painful stimulus; protective flexion; not clearly purposeful toward the stimulus source
   - Localizes to pain (Score 5): purposeful movement toward the site of stimulation; attempts to remove or push away the stimulus; indicates awareness of pain location
   - Visual cues: limb flexion away from stimulus (withdrawal) versus hand/arm movement directed toward stimulus location (localizes)

3: Obeys Commands / Normal (score 6)
   - Follows simple commands (e.g., open eyes, squeeze hand) or demonstrates appropriate, purposeful, commanded motor actions
   - Visual cues: cooperative, instructed actions; context-appropriate motor responses

